<title>UK: Gold sharply lower in Europe, seen consolidating. [corrected 08:40 gmt]</title>
<headline>Gold sharply lower in Europe, seen consolidating. [corrected 08:40 gmt]</headline>
<text>
<p>Gold - opened lower at $324.00/$324.50 versus $331.20/$331.80 at the London close. Mood remains overwhelmingly bearish (Corrects from bullish), but prices likely to consolidate with U.S. closed for holiday.</p>
<p>Silver - lower at $4.56/$4.58 from $4.64/$4.66.</p>
<p>Platinum - lower at $416.00/$420.00 versus $423.00/$428.00.</p>
<p>Palladium - easier at $187.00/$190.00 versus $189.50/$194.50.</p>
</text>
